  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure near overhead will allow for cold morning this\nmorning with temperatures in the mid 20s to low teens.\nTemperatures will rebound into the 50s today under sunny skies\nas high pressure settles south of the area. Rising heights and\nmodest warm air advection will continue the warming trend into\nMonday when much of the area will see highs in the 60s and\nsouthern locations pushing 70F.\n\nA cold front over SE Canada will attempt to push southward into\nthe area Tuesday that will bring more in the way of clouds and\nlow chances for showers, mainly across the north. Highs will\nlikely drop a few degrees from Monday's readings, but will\nremain mild in the 50s and 60s. This front will likely lift\nnorth of the area Wednesday leading to mostly dry conditions and\nhighs creeping upwards into the 60s. Troughing over the central\nUS will migrate east through the second half of the week while\nmodels suggest the trough will weaken as it does so.\nNevertheless, this trough will advect moisture into the region\nwith PoPs increasing Thursday into Friday. While a multi model\nconsensus suggest the Northeast will see some precipitation \nthese days and going into the weekend, confidence is low in the\nevolution of any low pressure systems or fronts that will drive\nthe precipitation. The pattern looks to remain unsettled going\ninto early next week.",
